PART 0b (PM-Q): quantum value G = 1 — Peres--Mermin operator identities (exact)
  [PASS] PM-Qa: all 6 line triples are jointly measurable (pairwise commuting)
  [PASS] PM-Qb: every line product is exactly +I or -I (operator identity)
  [PASS] PM-Qc: exactly one line has product -I (the parity obstruction)
  [PASS] PM-Qd: TARGETS[c] == sign(line product c) for all c (game matches the operators)
  Table (rows R0-R2, cols C0-C2): [('XX', 'XI', 'IX'), ('YY', 'XZ', 'ZX'), ('ZZ', 'IZ', 'ZI')]
  Line products: R0=+I, R1=+I, R2=+I, C0=-I, C1=+I, C2=+I
  => in ANY quantum state, measuring the three observables of line c gives outcomes
     whose product equals the target t_c with probability 1: quantum G = 1 (algebraic max).

